BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE:IU Bloomington Libraries
DTSTART:20261205T150000Z
DTEND:20261205T210000Z
LOCATION:WYLIE HOUSE (307 E. SECOND STREET)
GEO:39.161697;-86.5309
SUMMARY:Garlands & Greenery Open House at Wylie House Museum
DESCRIPTION:Wander through the historic house at your own pace\, surround
 ed by fresh greenery and traditional holiday decorations. Costumed staff 
 will be on hand to welcome you\, share stories\, and answer questions.  E
 njoy live music throughout the day\, featuring the Dickens Carolers\, IU 
 student musicians and á cappella groups\, and the Horseshoe Bend String 
 Band. In the Museum's Education Center\, warm up with hot cider and cocoa
 \, enjoy holiday cookies\, and try your hand at family-friendly craft act
 ivities.  Come celebrate the season with music\, merriment\, and the time
 less beauty of Wylie House Museum! No registration required.Parking: Desi
 gnated\, free Wylie House parking spots are located behind the museum and
  education center\, accessible via the alley. Free street parking is loca
 ted directly in front of the museum on 2nd St. and is permissible on Satu
 rdays in all the area neighborhood residential zoned spaces.Accessibility
 : The museum has accessible parking next to the museum's Morton C. Bradle
 y\, Jr. Education Center\, with a path that leads to a ramp at the back d
 oor entrance of the museum. While the historic home's second floor is onl
 y accessible by staircase\, digital images and virtual tour options are p
 rovided for visitors who cannot visit the second floor. Please contact us
  in advance of your visit to discuss any specific needs.  ***************
 ******************************************************************  Looki
 ng for a fully guided tour of the historic home? Visit Wylie House Museum
  on Friday\, December 4 (https://events.iu.edu/libraries/event/2441814-wi
 nter-holiday-tours-at-wylie-house-museum)\; Friday\, December 11 (https:/
 /events.iu.edu/libraries/event/2441815-winter-holiday-tours-at-wylie-hous
 e-museum)\; or Saturday\, December 12 (https://events.iu.edu/libraries/ev
 ent/2441816-winter-holiday-tours-at-wylie-house-museum). Free holiday sea
 son tours are offered at the top of each hour from 10 a.m. to 4 p.m.\, wi
 th the final tour beginning at 3 p.m.
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<p>  Wander through the historic house at yo
 ur own pace\, surrounded by fresh greenery and traditional holiday decora
 tions. Costumed staff will be on hand to welcome you\, share stories\, an
 d answer questions.</p><p>  Enjoy live music throughout the day\, featuri
 ng the Dickens Carolers\, IU student musicians and á cappella groups\, a
 nd the Horseshoe Bend String Band. In the Museum's Education Center\, war
 m up with hot cider and cocoa\, enjoy holiday cookies\, and try your hand
  at family-friendly craft activities.</p><p>  Come celebrate the season w
 ith music\, merriment\, and the timeless beauty of Wylie House Museum! No
  registration required.</p><p><strong>Parking:</strong> Designated\, free
  Wylie House parking spots are located behind the museum and education ce
 nter\, accessible via the alley. Free street parking is located directly 
 in front of the museum on 2nd St. and is permissible on Saturdays in all 
 the area neighborhood residential zoned spaces.</p><p><strong>Accessibili
 ty:</strong> The museum has accessible parking next to the museum's Morto
 n C. Bradley\, Jr. Education Center\, with a path that leads to a ramp at
  the back door entrance of the museum. While the historic home's second f
 loor is only accessible by staircase\, digital images and virtual tour op
 tions are provided for visitors who cannot visit the second floor. Please
  contact us in advance of your visit to discuss any specific needs.</p><p
 >  **********************************************************************
 ***********<br />  Looking for a fully guided tour of the historic home? 
 Visit Wylie House Museum on <a href="https://events.iu.edu/libraries/even
 t/2441814-winter-holiday-tours-at-wylie-house-museum">Friday\, December 4
 </a>\; <a href="https://events.iu.edu/libraries/event/2441815-winter-holi
 day-tours-at-wylie-house-museum">Friday\, December 11</a>\; or <a href="h
 ttps://events.iu.edu/libraries/event/2441816-winter-holiday-tours-at-wyli
 e-house-museum">Saturday\, December 12</a>. Free holiday season tours are
  offered at the top of each hour from 10 a.m. to 4 p.m.\, with the final 
 tour beginning at 3 p.m.</p>
